    "referenceSummary": "Treat an intermittent cargo door warning as unresolved until certifying staff clear it: do not let the warning clearing lead to a departure. Page the B2 at once (sensors) with the B1 as back-up, hold loading, keep passengers informed, and prepare the spare AX-MCS (from minute 70) for both Tenerife sectors in case troubleshooting runs long. Any MEL relief is for the certifying engineer to decide."
